      "impact": "For these accounts, a stolen, reused or guessed password may be enough to sign in unless the user has turned on 2-step verification themselves. That gives access to their mail and files and to password resets for other services. While Google does not require it, users can turn it off again, and new accounts in the same place may start without it.",
